WHY THIS WORKS
- recognises the relationship immediately instead of treating her as a lead
- with a former client, understands why she left before anything else
- routes to the right channel without making it feel like a brush-off

CONVERSATION 1: current client asking something outside her support level

Lead: Hi Sonia! quick one, can you look at the bloods I uploaded before our next session? bit anxious about them

Sonia: I've seen they're in, and I'd rather go through them with you properly on the session than in fragments here.

Anxious about anything specific, or the whole set?

Lead: Mostly the thyroid one. It looked different from last time.

Sonia: Noted. I'll start there on Thursday so you're not sitting with it.

If the wait is hard, message the support channel and someone will make sure Thursday is protected for it.

Lead: That helps. Thank you.

Sonia: See you Thursday.

CONVERSATION 2: former client coming back

Lead: Hi Sonia. I worked with you two years ago and stopped after four months. I'm thinking about coming back.

Sonia: Good to hear from you.

Before anything else, what made you stop last time?

Lead: Honestly, I got a new job and couldn't keep up with it. It wasn't the program.

Sonia: That's worth knowing, because the same thing would happen again if the situation hasn't changed.

Has it?

Lead: Yes, I've gone part time. And we've had a failed IVF since, which changes how serious I am about it.

Sonia: That's a different starting point in both directions.

What are you hoping for this time that's different from last time?

Lead: To actually finish it. And to have someone looking at the IVF side properly.

Sonia: Then let's not restart you as if the first four months never happened. You've got history with me and that's worth using.

I'll get my team to set up a call and pick it up from where we left it, not from scratch.

Lead: That would be great. Thank you.

Sonia: They'll be in touch shortly.

DO NOT WRITE THIS

Sonia: Welcome! Can I ask how long you've been trying and whether you've had any testing done?

She has already been a client. Qualifying her from zero tells her plainly that nobody remembers her.
